 "intro": "North of the Danube near Carnuntum (in modern Austria), 170 AD. Plague is killing Romans, and Marcus Aurelius has raised new troops from slaves and gladiators. You command his army against the Marcomanni.",
 "debrief": "The details are poorly recorded. Ancient writers say a Roman army was badly beaten, perhaps with 20,000 dead, and the Marcomanni and Quadi crossed the Alps into Italy, besieging Aquileia and burning Opitergium, the first invasion of Italy in centuries. A Praetorian Prefect was killed. Marcus Aurelius spent most of his remaining years fighting on the Danube, where he wrote his Meditations. The other choices are what-ifs.",
